  "notes": "{風化|ふうか} has both a geological and a metaphorical meaning.\n\nKANJI BREAKDOWN:\n- {風|ふう} (wind)\n- {化|か} (change, transform)\n\nSENSE 1 (Geological weathering):\n- {風化|ふうか}{作用|さよう} (weathering action/process)\n- {物理|ぶつり}{的|てき}{風化|ふうか} (physical weathering)\n- {化学|かがく}{的|てき}{風化|ふうか} (chemical weathering)\n\nSENSE 2 (Fading from memory):\nThis metaphorical usage is common in discussions about historical events, tragedies, or social issues.\n- {記憶|きおく}の{風化|ふうか} (fading of memory)\n- {風化|ふうか}させない (to not let something be forgotten)\n- {風化|ふうか}を{防|ふせ}ぐ (to prevent fading from memory)\n\nUSAGE:\n- {風化|ふうか}する (to weather; to fade from memory - suru verb)",
